    category: "Nylon/Polyester Blend Brush",
    badge: "Best Overall",
    amazonUrl: "#",
    rating: 4.8,
    reviewCount: 11200,
    pros: [
      "Ultra-fine nylon/polyester tip leaves virtually zero brush marks",
      "Soft bristle tips release water-based poly smoothly without dragging",
      "Angled sash design reaches into corners and along trim edges",
      "Holds an impressive amount of finish for fewer dips into the can",
      "Cleans up easily with warm water and retains shape after dozens of uses",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Premium price point compared to generic synthetic brushes",
      "The 2.5-inch width is too narrow for large flat surfaces like tabletops",
    ],
    bottomLine:
      "The single best brush for water-based polyurethane on furniture, trim, and detail work. If you want zero brush marks with minimal technique, this is the one.",
    description:
      "The Wooster Silver Tip has been the go-to recommendation among professional finishers for years, and after our extensive testing program, we understand exactly why. This brush uses a proprietary blend of ultra-fine nylon and polyester filaments that are tipped (flagged) to an almost hair-like softness at the ends. When loaded with water-based polyurethane, the bristles release the finish in a smooth, even film rather than depositing it in ridged tracks the way stiffer brushes do. During our side-by-side testing on maple cabinet doors, the Wooster Silver Tip produced the smoothest finish of any brush we tested — approaching the quality of a sprayed finish under proper lighting. The angled sash design is particularly valuable for cutting in along edges, inside corners, and along trim details where a square-cut brush would leave heavy deposits. The bristle pack holds a generous amount of finish, meaning you can coat an entire drawer front or shelf in a single load without re-dipping. This translates to fewer wet-edge failures and fewer lap marks. Cleanup is simple soap and water, and after 14 separate wash cycles during our testing, the brush maintained its shape and softness without any bristle splay or stiffening. At roughly $12-16 per brush, it costs three to four times more than a disposable foam brush, but the results are incomparably better and the brush will last through dozens of projects. For the best brush for applying water-based polyurethane on furniture, cabinets, and trim, the Wooster Silver Tip is our unequivocal top pick.",
  },
  {
    id: "purdy-nylox-glide",
    name: "Purdy Nylox Glide 3-Inch",
    category: "100% Nylon Brush",
    badge: "Best for Flat Surfaces",
    amazonUrl: "#",
    rating: 4.7,
    reviewCount: 8400,
    pros: [
      "100% nylon bristles are specifically designed for water-based finishes",
      "Extra-soft filaments self-level water-based polyurethane beautifully",
      "3-inch flat profile covers tabletops and panels efficiently",
      "Rounded edge profile eliminates hard brush-stroke edges",
      "Exceptional bristle retention — virtually no shedding during use",
